-- title:
--   One combined-charge capacity depth works for every admissible exceptional exponent
-- statement:
--   For every $c>C_0$ there is a natural depth $d\ge201$ such that for every real $\delta_*$ with $0<\delta_*<1/18$ and $C_{\rm exc}(c)\delta_*/\theta_{\rm exc}\le(c-C_0)/48$, the paper combined-charge terminal holds at depth d:
--
--   $$\exists d\ge201\ \forall\delta_*\text{ admissible},\quad\text{eventually in }n\text{ a compatible bank and guarded anchor certificate exist}. $$
--
--   They satisfy anchor-times-base divisibility into the central tail product, base-bank and combined-selector-charge divisibility into the precharged target, retained reserve $(c-C_0)n/[24(p-1)\log n]$ above the combined charge for primes $p\le2d+1$, and the exact selector-target-times-charge and precharged-target-times-anchor-divisor identities.
--
--   The depth is fixed before choosing the exceptional exponent; the eventual threshold may depend on that later exponent.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/ShouqiaoW/erdos/blob/61325b10bbdc29f4fb5e0618b414b9f2189333ad/390/lean/Erdos390/WholePaper/BankPaperCombinedChargeDepthFirstTerminal.lean#L74-L411

